    <bpmn:process id="W_W5106" name="W5106. Regional/District Territory Design, Alignment &amp; Store-Group Assignment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual review; new-store openings (VS-37); store closures (VS-59); workload imbalance
Frequency: Annual + event-driven
Volume: ~6 regions → ~10–15 districts → 200 store-group assignments
Owner: Director Field Retail Operations
Participants: Store Ops (VS-07), Strategy (VS-33), HR (VS-103), Supply Chain/DC (VS-02/VS-04 — DC catchment), Finance (VS-17.4)
Source: workflow W5106 — Regional/District Territory Design, Alignment &amp; Store-Group Assignment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5106_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5106_Lane1" name="Director Field Retail Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5106_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5106_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5106_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5106_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5106_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5106_Start3" name="Annual review; new-store openings (VS-37); store closures (VS-59); workload imbalance">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5106_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5106_Task4" name="Design territories by workload &amp; geography: stores-per-manager target…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Design territories by workload &amp; geography: stores-per-manager target, geographic clustering (island/region), DC catchment alignment (links VS-04 4-DC footprint), drive-time/travel-load balancing, and the regional/district naming convention
Responsible (R): Director Field Retail Operations / Strategy
Accountable (A): Director Field Retail Operations
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5106_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5106_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5106_Task5" name="Assign stores to territories: per-store group assignment, manager allocation…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Assign stores to territories: per-store group assignment, manager allocation, the transition plan for re-alignments, and the system master update (location hierarchy)
Responsible (R): Director Field Retail Operations / Store Ops / IT
Accountable (A): Director Field Retail Operations
Duration: Annual + event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5106_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5106_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5106_Task6" name="Validate balance &amp; re-balance triggers: workload equity check (sales, store…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Validate balance &amp; re-balance triggers: workload equity check (sales, store count, complexity, new-store load), the re-alignment threshold policy, and the quarterly balance review
Responsible (R): Director Field Retail Operations / Analytics
Accountable (A): Director Field Retail Operations
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5106_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5106_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5106_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5106_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-761 (ensure controlled execution — Field Organization, Territory Design &amp; Regional/District Store Management (PA-177.1).) | - CTL-761: territory design data-driven &amp; balanced; assignments reflected in location-hierarchy master (VS-29); re-balance threshold governed
Owner: Director Field Retail Operations</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5106_Assoc9" sourceRef="W5106_Annotation8" targetRef="W5106_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
